            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The diff in engine/cmd/review.go only extends the JSON output of review check: it adds an Exemptions field, initialises Results to an empty array, and copies the exemption fields (name, base, diff digest) from the checked value. The clearance logic that holds exemptions to their rules and to git sits in the app layer outside this candidate, so this change does not alter any authorization decision.",
              "The output exposes only repository-relative exemption file names, the base revision and a diff digest. These are data the caller already has access to, so there is no new secret or data exposure.",
              "The changes in bin/lib/usage.sh and engine/cmd/usage.go are help text only.",
              "engine/cmd/review_exempt_check_test.go is a new test file. It covers refusal of tampered exemptions: an edited risk, an edited report result, a wrong diff digest and an invalid stored file. It also covers a blocking result winning over an exemption. The tests write only to their own temporary world and add no dependencies.",
              "No reachable security, data-loss, unsafe-input or dependency risk was introduced by this candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
