            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/cmd/review.go: reportChecked now starts Results as an empty slice, so an exemption-only clearance prints \"results\": [] rather than null. A result-cleared head still lists the same entries as before. Exemptions use omitempty, so the output for heads cleared by results is unchanged.",
              "engine/cmd/review_exempt_check_test.go covers the new behavior at the cheapest useful levels. It asserts the exact stdout JSON, empty stderr, exit 0 and that nothing is stored for an exemption-only clearance. It checks that a blocking result or an unchecked severe finding wins over an exemption, with the refusal on stderr, an empty stdout and exit 1. It checks refusals for a never-exempted head, an exemption for another head, an edited risk, an edited report, a changed diff digest and an invalid file, each with no files stored. It adds a built-binary end-to-end flow and a usage-text test.",
              "The usage text assertions in engine/cmd/review_exempt_check_test.go match the strings added to engine/cmd/usage.go and bin/lib/usage.sh once whitespace is normalized with strings.Fields, so line wrapping does not break them.",
              "The clearance and refusal logic (checked.Exemptions, the exemption candidate fields) sits in the review application layer, which is outside this candidate. I could not verify it from this patch. The CLI layer only maps those fields to JSON, and the tests exercise them through the command, so I report no finding. Test setup also assumes the stored result takes number 2 after the exemption takes number 1, which I could not verify here."
            ]
          }
        }
